1. SCOPE AND EXISTING RIGHTS

This licence governs QualityLayer and the source, workflow instructions,
templates, schemas, documentation and assets distributed with it (the Software).
Public Source means only the material Maximilian Ritter deliberately releases
under this licence in the designated public source projection. Third-party
components retain their own licences and notices.

This licence applies prospectively to versions distributed with it. It does not
revoke, narrow or replace rights already granted under an earlier licence or a
separately agreed contract, including existing Enterprise complete-source,
modification and derivative-work rights. An individual agreement prevails to
the extent of a conflict. Existing contractual prices, currencies, seats,
benefits, grants, licence keys, activations and access continue under their
agreed terms. Pilot Shell 11 remains governed by its applicable licence.
No automatic conversion to another licence or free product edition occurs.

2. OFFICIAL PRODUCT USE

An applicable seven-day trial, active subscription or previously granted right
permits the assigned person to use the official QualityLayer App and CLI on
machines they own or control for personal or internal commercial work. Each
person using the product needs an assigned licence. The current activation limit
and offline allowance continue unchanged: a key works on five computers; after
a successful licence check, the offline allowance is up to seven days. This does
not create a perpetual-use right after a trial or subscription expires.

The trial starts on first use, once per computer, and requires no payment.
An upgrade or backend migration does not restart an existing trial. Continued
use after the trial requires a subscription unless previously granted rights
provide otherwise. Cancellation ends renewal; access continues through the paid
period under the applicable terms.

Individual licenses one person. Business provides the same complete local
product per person, centralized seats and billing, licence assignment and
reassignment, priority support and priority consideration of feature requests.
Priority consideration promises no implementation or delivery date. Enterprise
includes Business and the volume, onboarding, invoicing, purchasing and support
terms separately agreed. The new offering includes no hosted collaboration
workspace, self-hosted team backend, SSO, private-source access or complete-build
grant. Previously granted rights remain protected by section 1.

Polar handles purchase, payment, invoices, tax and renewal as merchant of record
under the terms shown at purchase. Prices for new purchases are shown at
https://qualitylayer.dev/pricing; they do not amend existing prices.

3. PUBLIC INSPECTION AND CONTRIBUTIONS

Whether or not you subscribe, you may:
(a) read Public Source to understand, inspect, evaluate and audit QualityLayer;
(b) retain copies and create and host contribution forks;
(c) edit those copies and run the explicitly documented focused public-component
    checks with synthetic data; and
(d) submit issues, patches and pull requests to improve QualityLayer itself.

Keep this licence and original notices with permitted copies, forks and patches.
Public contribution forks and patches are permitted for that contribution
purpose. These express permissions override any general restriction on copying,
modification, publication or derivative works in this licence to the extent
necessary for these activities. They do not require a subscription and do not
end merely because a subscription expires.

Incorporating a contribution requires the Contribution Submission Agreement in
CONTRIBUTING.md. Ordinary discussion, a bug report or material clearly marked
for discussion alone is not acceptance for unrelated or unsubmitted code.

4. PRIVATE COMPONENTS AND COMPLETE BUILDS

Public Source includes nonlicensing application behavior, agent execution,
permissions, approvals, data handling, workflow instructions and composition.
Official releases bundle their matching workflow assets locally. Published
instructions are not confidential. Permission to run the commercial product is
separate from permission to inspect its instructions.

Private licensing/trial enforcement, the commercial backend, internal CI/CD,
operations and complete-build/protection/signing implementation are outside the
public projection. No private source, credentials, decryption/signing keys,
proprietary replacement package or complete-build permission is granted.
Public checks exercise isolated components and contracts. The public checkout
intentionally lacks inputs needed to build the complete application.

Only Maximilian Ritter produces complete official builds, directly or through
automation under his control. This does not narrow section 1 or mandatory law.

5. RESTRICTIONS

Except for sections 1 and 3, separately agreed permission, third-party licence
rights or mandatory law, you may not:
(a) redistribute, sell, sublicense or offer a standalone or rebranded Software
    version or derivative product;
(b) incorporate QualityLayer source, workflow instructions or assets into another
    product or service, or distribute them independently of a permitted
    QualityLayer contribution fork or patch;
(c) offer the Software as a hosted service to other people;
(d) independently assemble, run or distribute a complete application outside the
    official product-use permission;
(e) bypass entitlement, activation, subscription or copy-protection enforcement,
    or provide a replacement implementation to remove those controls;
(f) remove proprietary notices or imply that a fork or contribution is an
    official release or endorsement through QualityLayer names or marks; or
(g) obtain private material or credentials without authorization.

These restrictions concern use of the Software, not independent implementation
of ideas copyright does not protect. They apply only as permitted by law.
Nothing restricts acts permitted notwithstanding contractual terms, including
nonwaivable backup, observation, study, testing and interoperability rights
under sections 69d, 69e and 69g UrhG.

