7. EXPIRY, BREACH AND CHANGES

Product-use permission ends with the applicable trial or subscription, subject
to offline terms and previously granted rights. Expiry alone does not end
section 3, require deletion of permitted Public Source copies or submitted
patches, or affect your own output.

A material breach may terminate the affected permission after notice and a
reasonable opportunity to remedy where applicable. Mandatory law, surviving
contribution grants, existing contractual rights and your output remain
unaffected. Licence changes do not retroactively remove granted rights.
New terms apply only to the extent validly agreed.

8. LIABILITY AND MANDATORY PROTECTION

We are liable without limit for intent and gross negligence, injury to life,
